[Start "italian-quiet-fourths 4.O-O Nf6"]

5. c3 { Prepares d4, which would hit the bishop on c5 and take the centre. } ( 5. Nc3 d6 ) ( 5. Re1 d6 { Gives e5 a pawn defender, so the rook on e1 has nothing to hit. } 6. c3 Bb6 { Steps back before d4 can hit the bishop with a gain of time. } ) ( 5. d4 Bxd4 { White's pawn on d4 was not defended enough. Black takes it and keeps an extra pawn. } 6. Nxd4 Nxd4 7. f4 ( 7. Bg5 h6 8. Bh4 d6 ) 7... d6 { Keeps the e5 pawn guarded. Black is a pawn up; White has quicker development and the f-file in return. } 8. fxe5 dxe5 9. Bg5 Qe7 ) ( 5. Ng5 O-O 6. d3 ) 5... Bb6 { Steps back before d4 can hit the bishop. On b6 it still aims at f2 and presses on d4. } 6. d4 ( 6. d3 d6 { The quiet Giuoco Piano set-up: next ...O-O, ...h6 and ...Ne7-g6 or ...Be6. } ) 6... d6 { Holds e5 with a pawn. If White takes on e5, Black takes back and the position opens with Black fully developed. Plan: castle, ...h6 to keep the c1 bishop off g5, and ...Bg4 or ...Re8 to press on White's centre. } *
